  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Local and Indigenous Knowledge holders supported to participate in environmental and climate change processes and activities, including in UNESCO Sites in Peruvian Amazonia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The lack of direct participation by Indigenous Peoples in the management of UNESCO-designated sites and other protected areas in the Amazonia undermines their rights and the conservation and sustainable development of these critical territories.  This activity will contribute to the implementation of the IberoMAB Action Framework for improving indigenous and Afrodescendant rights in UNESCO designated sites particularly under the REDLAC follow up. I will entail mobilizing additional funds and working together in Peru with Indigenous Peoples&apos; Organizations and other national and regional stakeholders including the Ministry of Environment and the Vice Ministry of Interculturality in charge of the portfolio.</narrative>
  </description>
